#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166665 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d83ab99-0e27-5989-9a57-6b4a192fa4a4" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability at a Point"}] :question/id #uuid "e3df676d-e1cc-584e-8b14-a6191a8d6831" :question/math-academy-id "e-8553" :question/problem "Given $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right),$ compute $P(X = 3).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n![](images/60/6044f7e9a7a3e784da6affc47c4cfcedce461feb44057992f39fd3154e5cb846.svg)\n\nHere, $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n![](images/d4/d4788968ba8347e6288028e679a0df0c3629c292aaca4552293fc6f9380486ef.svg)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=3) & =f(3) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}(\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166666 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "120381af-c472-5894-8b19-da2ab61d3a7e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over a Bounded Interval: Lower Bound is Zero"}] :question/id #uuid "f795e566-5cdf-5970-bf94-5b1c838b69f1" :question/math-academy-id "e-8554" :question/problem "Given $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac 37\\right),$ compute $P(X < 5).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n![](images/f6/f6da43d5d0276991429f04048f3ea4e7ec2b4d9727abc71f4d7879cefd71797b.svg)\n\nHere, $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac 37\\right),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n![](images/bc/bcba51c019bfe72f14e0fb7d6465abf3595b03c8e70598231934f5166393873b.svg)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{4}{7})}^{0}(\\frac{3}{7})+{(\\frac{4}{7})}^{1}(\\frac{3}{7})+{(\\frac{4}{7})}^{2}(\\frac{3}{7})+{(\\frac{4}{7})}^{3}(\\frac{3}{7}) \\\\  & ≈0.893\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto  $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166667 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166829 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c566525f-9b0f-586f-ba60-277400cb25dd" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over a Bounded Interval: Lower Bound is Not Zero"}] :question/id #uuid "c23e8b4a-dad2-5c6a-95ee-2a439343ded0" :question/math-academy-id "e-8555" :question/problem "Given that $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac 15\\right),$ compute $P(2 \\leq X \\leq 3).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n![](images/8f/8fe2487af4333bae81059a2ab221b3988bbdf27f4f51521683addd789c31a4b9.svg)\n\nHere, $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac 15\\right),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n![](images/a4/a44212ab1418417646876630a4cea241bfefaf063b26251dc5f157824cc4805d.svg)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2\\le X\\le 3) & =P(X\\in \\{2,3\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{4}{5})}^{1}(\\frac{1}{5})+{(\\frac{4}{5})}^{2}(\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{125}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166668 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "215130d1-96ea-5f88-8de0-d73758ea8344" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over a Bounded Interval Using the Complement"}] :question/id #uuid "c798d6ea-a258-5a73-8cd2-366e1b3e9db0" :question/math-academy-id "e-8556" :question/problem "Given $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac 56\\right),$ compute $P(X > 2).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n![](images/0d/0d3d01e8f77c51e75d7dfce4ef2b60e8a61be89eaf752b2203857d97e77c6127.svg)\n\nHere, $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac 56\\right),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n![](images/db/db0084ae705309592c8d309304e26a46ecde6e6a1b85ef07b57b6f1a394f26fa.svg)\n\nThere are infinitely many values of $X$ such that $X > 2.$ However, we can simplify the computation by using the complement instead:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>2) & =1-P(X\\le 2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{6})}^{0}(\\frac{5}{6})+{(\\frac{1}{6})}^{1}(\\frac{5}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>2) & =1-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{35}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490311 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d83ab99-0e27-5989-9a57-6b4a192fa4a4" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f1f34bb-a03a-5956-8592-2d5b964b0260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1029" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489801} {:answer/id #uuid "9ef3d34e-9394-51e7-ab15-87526ccf7d58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0057" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489867} {:answer/id #uuid "a4b66f29-5a42-52a3-be66-da30a8d25610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0081" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489881} {:answer/id #uuid "aefa0635-700b-51ba-af5e-be1ad507b89c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.027" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489898} {:answer/id #uuid "d97464cd-bf5a-577a-9847-a99a3c83a3fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0189" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d97464cd-bf5a-577a-9847-a99a3c83a3fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0189" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489994} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2f3772d-82b4-52de-abe3-8e3cd1b9192d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490186}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ddebff9a-c321-5053-81a7-09bc2befcfb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-130032" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.7),$ compute $P(X=4).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.7),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(0.3)}^{x-1}(0.7), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=4) & =f(4) \\\\  & ={(0.3)}^{3}(0.7) \\\\  & =0.0189.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490238 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d83ab99-0e27-5989-9a57-6b4a192fa4a4" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12719200-e104-56e8-b712-c638a73fe46f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0749" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489556} {:answer/id #uuid "5d21d304-740b-5376-a2c8-3fcb5c2851e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1664" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489737} {:answer/id #uuid "73793f7d-9072-5da6-abd4-390066e06095" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0501" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489786} {:answer/id #uuid "924cd6fa-d634-5f0d-8aca-01b2e778a480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0412" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489845} {:answer/id #uuid "c88e1276-0a5c-53af-a35b-40bf38708c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0915" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12719200-e104-56e8-b712-c638a73fe46f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0749" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489556} :answer-field/id #uuid "505f0222-4cef-53e2-a6b9-3e430e0cccd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490122}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3c3e7bcc-b40d-5576-a6ae-56d69405dfc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-130033" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.45),$ compute $P(X=4).$  Round your final answer to $4$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.45),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(0.55)}^{x-1}(0.45), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=4) & =f(4) \\\\  & ={(0.55)}^{3}(0.45) \\\\  & ≈0.0749.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490215 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "215130d1-96ea-5f88-8de0-d73758ea8344" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over a Bounded Interval Using the Complement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f4f0d37-31fa-580f-a61f-73b377587e0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2041" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489549} {:answer/id #uuid "57493273-713c-5bd8-9c9d-be6b143d9126" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9184" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489722} {:answer/id #uuid "65c9f129-b21a-5d19-8e36-b0303bd7567e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7959" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489755} {:answer/id #uuid "c75df401-1338-550f-9685-bdbf40c3f545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0816" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489945} {:answer/id #uuid "cbf65f81-805f-53f1-bb8a-3704c0abd456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1837" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c75df401-1338-550f-9685-bdbf40c3f545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0816" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489945} :answer-field/id #uuid "5526fa50-a4a2-58c4-84bf-0839d0ec3ffd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490125}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "075d366c-d06a-5f72-a1db-49d33772eb88" :question/math-academy-id "q-130234" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{5}{7}),$ compute $P(X\\ge 3)$ rounded to $4$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{5}{7}),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{2}{7})}^{x-1}(\\frac{5}{7}), & x=1,2,3… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are infinitely many values of $X$ such that $X\\ge 3.$ However, we can simplify the computation by using the complement instead:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 3) & =1-P(X<3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<3) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{7})}^{0}(\\frac{5}{7})+{(\\frac{2}{7})}^{1}(\\frac{5}{7}) \\\\  & ≈0.9184.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 3) & =1-P(X<3) \\\\  & ≈1-0.9184 \\\\  & =0.0816.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490240 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "215130d1-96ea-5f88-8de0-d73758ea8344" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over a Bounded Interval Using the Complement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09dd5e08-c7b9-5be8-a4d3-f4cc107331c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.099" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489536} {:answer/id #uuid "10deaade-3a9c-5ec3-bc56-7264acd0d86c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.999" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489554} {:answer/id #uuid "322e9559-5dc4-5f4e-9715-244d5740f1d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.901" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489627} {:answer/id #uuid "388a44e1-09c9-5049-b06d-9b541bad14cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0001" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489641} {:answer/id #uuid "81f8b757-ab50-560b-84f0-4b171b81f5da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.001" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "388a44e1-09c9-5049-b06d-9b541bad14cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0001" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489641} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cf79bbd-87e9-5932-996b-d7506f0bd20e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490087}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "409b1f60-69c1-5499-92f9-7ef6676bbb2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-130240" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.9),$ compute $P(X>4).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.9),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(0.1)^{x-1}(0.9), & x=1,2,3… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are infinitely many values of $X$ such that $X>4.$ However, we can simplify the computation by using the complement instead:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>4) & =1-P(X\\le 4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 4) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & =(0.1)^{0}(0.9)+(0.1)^{1}(0.9)+(0.1)^{2}(0.9)+(0.1)^{3}(0.9) \\\\  & =0.9999.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>4) & =1-P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =1-0.9999 \\\\  & =0.0001.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490300 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "215130d1-96ea-5f88-8de0-d73758ea8344" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over a Bounded Interval Using the Complement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35185109-1abd-547a-b4ce-7323baa540c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.008" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35185109-1abd-547a-b4ce-7323baa540c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.008" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489634} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b68151b-043e-5564-8a91-ea873b4fca7a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c2bbdab6-51f8-5199-a746-5b96164dbacd" :question/math-academy-id "q-276116" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.8),$ compute the **exact** value of $P(X>3).$\n\n$P(X>3)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.9),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(0.2)^{x-1}(0.8), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are infinitely many values of $X$ such that $X>3.$ However, we can simplify the computation by using the complement instead:\n\n$$\nP(X>3)=1-P(X\\le 3)\n$$\n\nComputing the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & =(0.2)^{0}(0.8)+(0.2)^{1}(0.8)+(0.2)^{2}(0.8) \\\\  & =0.992.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>3) & =1-P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =1-0.992 \\\\  & =0.008.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490218 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "120381af-c472-5894-8b19-da2ab61d3a7e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over a Bounded Interval: Lower Bound is Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23d401c2-e965-5c1f-bf12-a1405281691f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9961" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23d401c2-e965-5c1f-bf12-a1405281691f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9961" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489597} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b3f1a70-503f-52c2-860a-0c47acfaab21" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "17f155c2-ce06-547c-8fc5-5b0b0c48ed1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-329137" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.75),$ compute $P(X<5).$ Round your final answer to $4$ decimal places.\n\n$P(X<5)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.75),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(0.25)^{x-1}(0.75), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & =(0.25)^{0}(0.75)+(0.25)^{1}(0.75)+(0.25)^{2}(0.75)+(0.25)^{3}(0.75) \\\\  & ≈0.9961.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490272 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d83ab99-0e27-5989-9a57-6b4a192fa4a4" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec06b592-8251-5caa-8800-efc045e64f99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{64}{625}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec06b592-8251-5caa-8800-efc045e64f99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{64}{625}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490025} :answer-f