85 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da4631ee-615f-5d28-ba69-71a6d6cc3214" :question/math-academy-id "q-332366" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{1}{2}),$ compute $P(X=6).$  Round your final answer to $4$ decimal places.\n\n$P(X=6)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{1}{2}),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x-1}(\\frac{1}{2}), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=6) & =f(6) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{5}(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & ≈0.0156.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490319 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166829 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c566525f-9b0f-586f-ba60-277400cb25dd" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over a Bounded Interval: Lower Bound is Not Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9663b4c1-0d09-501b-85ec-b12bc71c403b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2436}{15625}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9663b4c1-0d09-501b-85ec-b12bc71c403b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2436}{15625}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489851} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f07629a-b94e-5918-a076-295a6afd6ca9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490147}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ebe82800-a8b2-58e9-ab4c-047410ac5d4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-332934" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{3}{5}),$ compute the **exact** value of $P(3\\le X\\le 6).$\n\n$P(3\\le X\\le 6)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{3}{5}),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{x-1}(\\frac{3}{5}), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3\\le X\\le 6) & =P(X\\in \\{3,4,5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=3)+P(X=4)+P(X=5)+P(X=6) \\\\  & =f(3)+f(4)+f(5)+f(6) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{5})}^{2}(\\frac{3}{5})+{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{3}(\\frac{3}{5})+{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{4}(\\frac{3}{5})+{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{5}(\\frac{3}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2436}{15625}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490317 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166829 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c566525f-9b0f-586f-ba60-277400cb25dd" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over a Bounded Interval: Lower Bound is Not Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b2c097b-83d9-5335-adb4-b351e48449d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3845" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b2c097b-83d9-5335-adb4-b351e48449d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3845" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489859} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6583c9a-95dc-5a97-93ac-4ed54bc666d0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e519920d-4b78-559e-a669-c1163fd46764" :question/math-academy-id "q-334517" :question/problem "Given that $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.25),$ compute $P(3\\le X<7)$ rounded to $4$ decimal places.\n\n$P(3\\le X<7)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.25),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(0.75)^{x-1}(0.25), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3\\le X<7) & =P(X\\in \\{3,4,5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=3)+P(X=4)+P(X=5)+P(X=6) \\\\  & =f(3)+f(4)+f(5)+f(6) \\\\  & =(0.75)^{2}(0.25)+(0.75)^{3}(0.25)+(0.75)^{4}(0.25)+(0.75)^{5}(0.25) \\\\  & ≈0.3845.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490243 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "120381af-c472-5894-8b19-da2ab61d3a7e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over a Bounded Interval: Lower Bound is Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e780059-1688-570a-b234-233305003b4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9610" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e780059-1688-570a-b234-233305003b4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9610" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489836} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdcc3e6a-dcfa-5751-a590-4c15ac84e072" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "458360eb-fd03-5244-aa64-17cd1909b422" :question/math-academy-id "q-335471" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{5}{9}),$ compute $P(X<5).$ Round your final answer to $4$ decimal places.\n\n$P(X<5)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{5}{9}),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{4}{9})}^{x-1}(\\frac{5}{9}), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{4}{9})}^{0}(\\frac{5}{9})+{(\\frac{4}{9})}^{1}(\\frac{5}{9})+{(\\frac{4}{9})}^{2}(\\frac{5}{9})+{(\\frac{4}{9})}^{3}(\\frac{5}{9}) \\\\  & ≈0.9610.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490302 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "120381af-c472-5894-8b19-da2ab61d3a7e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over a Bounded Interval: Lower Bound is Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b76c2ecd-bfe3-572f-9e1c-e2783e3ff672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{255}{256}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b76c2ecd-bfe3-572f-9e1c-e2783e3ff672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{255}{256}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489919} :answer-field/id #uuid "374164b9-fa8d-5f84-b049-4c4079513c6a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490105}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c5de4d6c-cfeb-57f1-bb0f-e9ef45447169" :question/math-academy-id "q-335472" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{3}{4}),$ compute the **exact** value of $P(X<5).$\n\n$P(X<5)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{3}{4}),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{x-1}(\\frac{3}{4}), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{4})}^{0}(\\frac{3}{4})+{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{1}(\\frac{3}{4})+{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}(\\frac{3}{4})+{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{3}(\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{255}{256}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "215130d1-96ea-5f88-8de0-d73758ea8344" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over a Bounded Interval Using the Complement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30f0c895-ef08-58e6-9075-734c56d0693f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0156" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30f0c895-ef08-58e6-9075-734c56d0693f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0156" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489624} :answer-field/id #uuid "97d7b59f-a2d2-58e3-a418-18885daa2bc6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490158}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "04c3981e-56b1-51ed-b49e-4d2d764aacc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-335508" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{7}{8}),$ compute $P(X\\ge 3)$ round to $4$ decimal places.\n\n$P(X\\ge 3)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{7}{8}),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{1}{8})}^{x-1}(\\frac{7}{8}), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are infinitely many values of $X$ such that $X\\ge 3.$ However, we can simplify the computation by using the complement instead:\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 3)=1-P(X<3)\n$$\n\nComputing the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<3) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{8})}^{0}(\\frac{7}{8})+{(\\frac{1}{8})}^{1}(\\frac{7}{8}) \\\\  & =0.984375.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 3) & =1-P(X<3) \\\\  & =1-0.984375 \\\\  & ≈0.0156.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490325 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "215130d1-96ea-5f88-8de0-d73758ea8344" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over a Bounded Interval Using the Complement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4da4c70c-df85-5925-90f4-b8d117992ed7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1296" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4da4c70c-df85-5925-90f4-b8d117992ed7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1296" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489697} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3e9dd74-0fb3-5ffa-8777-7735bf525da5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f9e4e9da-f36b-5b4a-91a7-731a48c88c99" :question/math-academy-id "q-335524" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.4),$ compute the **exact** value of $P(X>4).$\n\n$P(X>4)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.4),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(0.6)^{x-1}(0.4), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are infinitely many values of $X$ such that $X>4.$ However, we can simplify the computation by using the complement instead:\n\n$$\nP(X>4)=1-P(X\\le 4)\n$$\n\nComputing the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 4) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & =(0.6)^{0}(0.4)+(0.6)^{1}(0.4)+(0.6)^{2}(0.4)+(0.6)^{3}(0.4) \\\\  & =0.8704.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>4) & =1-P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =1-0.8704 \\\\  & =0.1296.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490323 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d83ab99-0e27-5989-9a57-6b4a192fa4a4" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "033c65a9-0b6e-5617-bdf6-d1c79c11ea62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489521} {:answer/id #uuid "1988de02-4c76-594d-8656-c6c044ffadbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489570} {:answer/id #uuid "2dcd0755-ff5f-51d8-a229-166b71f1ef18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489616} {:answer/id #uuid "dff4f121-9d79-55a3-91b8-351004a0cd79"